<span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-family: 'quattrocento sans';">Since the establishment of the preserve, Washington Island school children have planted hundreds of native trees and shrubs to enhance </span><span style="font-family: 'quattrocento sans';">the property’s bird habitat. Avian visitors include eastern kingbirds, field sparrows, meadowlarks and bluebirds. Kestrels, harriers and other birds of prey may be seen hunting in these open meadows. </span></span>

